# Cloudflare Pages headers — kill the Edge/Safari stale-cache problem.
# HTML must always revalidate (so a deploy shows up on the next refresh in
# EVERY browser); the service worker file too. Hashed/versioned assets can
# cache hard.

# Security headers on every response. These are the non-breaking hardening set;
# a strict Content-Security-Policy is intentionally NOT here yet — it needs
# testing against the inline scripts, Google Identity Services, the html2pdf CDN
# and the Gemini calls before it can go on without breaking the app.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

